              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क्या कहा? (kyā kahā?) — \"what did you say?\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कहा is the past of कहना, \"to say\". Short, and fine among friends; with a stranger, add जी."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क्या कहा? (kyā kahā?) is \"what was said?\". kahnā, \"to say\", comes from Sanskrit kathayati, \"converses with, describes\" (CDIAL 2703)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A quick request to hear it again."
